\[(z - 2) - (z - 2)^2 - 2 = 0,\]so
\[(z - 2)^2 - z + 4 = 0.\]Let
\[t = x^4,\]so
\[t - (t - z)^2 - t + 4 = 0,\]or
\[-t^2 + (2z - 1)t + 4 = 0.\]This factors as $[t - (2z - 1)] (t + 4) = 0.$  Since $t = x^4$ is positive, the root $t = \frac{1 - 2z}{t}$, so
\[x = \sqrt{\frac{1 - 2z}{t}}.\]If the root of $t$ is $\frac{1 - 2z}{4},$ then the squares of the roots of $x$ differ by $2 \cdot \frac{1 - 2z}{4} = \boxed{\frac{1}{4}}.$  Note that this is independent of $z.$

